# R47 Track B — PER-ARM POSITIVE CONTROL for the COMPENSATION that makes the
# adapter arms safe to convert.
#
# CELL: arm = combinator adapter, `Callable[T]`-PARAMETER branch
# (`methods.rs`, `__callable_N` inside `call_closure_in_adapter`) ·
# combinator = `Option.unwrap_or_else` on the None path · payload = String.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS THE ARM A PRIOR REVIEW READ AS "ACCIDENTALLY CLEAN". Its probe was
# reported CLEAN by a harness that greps only for LeakSanitizer's summary
# line; the same probe was in fact aborting with an ASan STACK-BUFFER-OVERFLOW
# that the harness never looked for. The overflow is a separate, still-open
# defect (the adapter infers `Option[i64]` for the result when the closure is
# a type-erased `Callable` parameter, then the caller reads the slot as
# `Option[String]`) — `unwrap_or_else` is used here precisely because it takes
# its result type from the receiver rather than from that inference, so this
# fixture exercises the arm without tripping the unrelated bug.
#
# RED-VERIFIED: with the register-at-birth conversion applied but the
# tracker-side transfer in `assign_result_local_move` REMOVED, this program
# aborts under ASan with `attempting double-free`, 3/3 runs. CLEAN 3/3 at
# pristine `f3feea79` and CLEAN 3/3 with the full change.
#
# The argument is a NAMED FUNCTION so the fixture is not contaminated by the
# separate `__gorget_closure_env_alloc` leak.
#
# INSTRUMENT: `security_safe_no_leak`, C lane only.
String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

String maker():
    return mk("hel", "lo")

String pick(Callable[String()] f):
    Option[String] o = None()
    return o.unwrap_or_else(f)

void main():
    print(pick(maker))
